Why Is Demand Increasing?
Growing vehicle ownership: Rising vehicle registrations expand the potential customer base for compulsory and optional insurance coverage.
Mandatory insurance requirements: Regulatory requirements in many markets support demand for third-party liability policies.
Digital insurance and telematics: Online distribution, automated claims processes, and usage-based pricing are helping insurers improve customer access and risk assessment.

Insurance Technology Watch: Telematics and Usage-Based Pricing
Motor vehicle insurers are increasingly using connected-car data, mobile applications, and telematics devices to assess driving behavior and personalize premiums. Digital policy issuance and claims tracking can also improve convenience for customers. However, insurers must manage repair-cost inflation, fraudulent claims, pricing volatility, data privacy, and the cost of modernizing legacy systems.

